IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cat-domain`
IMPORT `cat-time`
IMPORT `cat-part1-preliminary`
IMPORT `cat-part2-div2-3-microchip-sterilise`

-- Cat Act 2011 (WA) — PART 2 DIVISION 1: REGISTRATION AND TAGGING (ss 5-13),
-- with Cat Regulations 2012 regs 9-16. Fees (Sch 3) are in
-- cat-regs-sch3-fees.l4; reg 12(2)(a), the length of a registration, is with
-- the s 3(1) definition of "registered" in cat-part1-preliminary.l4.
--
-- Source: inputs/cat-act-2011.txt lines 202-279; inputs/cat-regulations-2012.txt
-- lines 112-185.

§ `Part 2 — Registration, identification and sterilisation of cats`

§§ `Division 1 — Registration and tagging`

§§§ `Subdivision 1 — Cats must be registered and tagged`

§§§§ `reg 9. Cats exempt from registration (s. 5(2)(c) and 9(2)(b))`

-- reg 9(1): "SAFE entity means any of the following — (a) Saving Animals from
-- Euthanasia Incorporated ...; (b) S.A.F.E. Hedland Inc ...; (c) Saving
-- Animals from Euthanasia Busselton Inc ...".
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 reg 9(1)
GIVEN o IS AN Organisation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a SAFE entity` o IF
        "(a)" ... o EQUALS `Saving Animals from Euthanasia Incorporated`
    ..  "(b)" ... o EQUALS `S.A.F.E. Hedland Inc`
    OR  "(c)" ... o EQUALS `Saving Animals from Euthanasia Busselton Inc`

-- reg 9(2): "a cat that is in the custody of any of the following is exempt
-- from registration — (a) Cat Haven; (b) the RSPCA WA; (c) the Department of
-- State of the Commonwealth that is administered by the Commonwealth Minister
-- administering the Biosecurity Act 2015 (Commonwealth); (d) a cat
-- management facility; (e) veterinary premises as defined in the Veterinary
-- Practice Act 2021 section 3."
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 reg 9(2)
GIVEN c IS A Custodian
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a custodian listed in reg 9(2)` c IF
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `an organisation` o THEN
                "(a)" ... o EQUALS `Cat Welfare Society Inc., trading as Cat Haven`
            ..  "(b)" ... o EQUALS `The Royal Society for the Prevention of Cruelty to Animals, Western Australia`
            OR  "(c)" ... o EQUALS `the Commonwealth Department administering the Biosecurity Act 2015`
    WHEN `a cat management facility` THEN TRUE      -- (d)
    WHEN `veterinary premises`       THEN TRUE      -- (e)
    WHEN `a private person`          THEN FALSE

-- reg 9(3): "a cat that is in foster care is exempt from registration if —
-- (a) the cat has been placed into that foster care by either of the
-- following — (i) Cat Haven; (ii) the RSPCA WA; or (b) the cat has been placed
-- into that foster care by a SAFE entity, provided that the cat has not been
-- in foster care for more than a total of 12 weeks."
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 reg 9(3)
GIVEN fp IS A `Foster placement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a foster placement within reg 9(3)` fp IF
        "(a)" ... `placed by Cat Haven or the RSPCA`
    OR  "(b)" ... `placed by a SAFE entity, for no more than 12 weeks`
    WHERE
        `placed by Cat Haven or the RSPCA` MEANS
                "(i)"  ... fp's `placed by` EQUALS `Cat Welfare Society Inc., trading as Cat Haven`
            OR  "(ii)" ... fp's `placed by` EQUALS `The Royal Society for the Prevention of Cruelty to Animals, Western Australia`
        `placed by a SAFE entity, for no more than 12 weeks` MEANS
                `a SAFE entity` (fp's `placed by`)
            AND "provided that the cat has not been in foster care for more than a total of 12 weeks"
            ... fp's `total weeks in foster care` AT MOST 12

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 5(2)(c), s 9(2)(b); Cat Regulations 2012 reg 9
GIVEN cat IS A Cat
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `belongs to a class of cats prescribed as exempt from registration` cat IF
        "reg 9(2)" ... `in a listed custody`
    OR  "reg 9(3)" ... `in a listed foster placement`
    WHERE
        `in a listed custody` MEANS
            CONSIDER cat's `custodian`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST c  THEN `a custodian listed in reg 9(2)` c
        `in a listed foster placement` MEANS
            CONSIDER cat's `foster placement`
            WHEN NOTHING  THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST fp  THEN `a foster placement within reg 9(3)` fp

§§§§ `5. Cats to be registered`

-- s 5(1): "The owner of a cat that has reached 6 months of age must ensure
-- that the cat is registered with the local government in whose district
-- the cat is ordinarily kept."
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 5(1)
GIVEN cat IS A Cat
      d   IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `registered with the local government of the district where it is ordinarily kept` cat `on` d IF
    `registered` cat `on` d
    AND CONSIDER cat's `registration`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST r  THEN r's `local government` EQUALS cat's `district where ordinarily kept`

-- s 5(2): "Subsection (1) does not apply if — (a) the cat has been kept by
-- the person for less than 14 days; or (b) the person has been resident in
-- the State for less than 14 days; or (c) the cat belongs to a class of cats
-- prescribed as exempt from registration."
--
-- FORK F-06: "kept by the person" — the person's own keeping where they have
-- one; an owner who keeps the cat only through someone else (a parent under
-- s 4(1)(c), a database-recorded owner under s 4(2)) is read as having kept
-- it for as long as the earliest current keeper has. "for less than 14 days"
-- counts whole days from the start of keeping (s 61(1)(b)): kept since
-- 1 October, the person has kept it for 14 days on 15 October.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 5(2)
GIVEN d   IS A DATE
      p   IS A Person
      cat IS A Cat
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(1) does not apply on` d `to` p `as to` cat IF
        "(a)" ... `the days the cat has been kept by the person` LESS THAN 14
    ..  "(b)" ... (Day d MINUS Day (p's `resident in the State since`)) LESS THAN 14
    OR  "(c)" ... `belongs to a class of cats prescribed as exempt from registration` cat
    WHERE
        `current keepings` MEANS filter (GIVEN k YIELD k's `since` AT MOST d) (cat's `keepings`)
        `the person's own` MEANS filter (GIVEN k YIELD k's `keeper`'s `name` EQUALS p's `name`) `current keepings`
        -- the prelude's `minimum` of a NUMBER list has no answer for an empty one
        `earliest start of` ks MEANS
            IF   null ks
            THEN Day d
            ELSE minimum (map (GIVEN k YIELD Day (k's `since`)) ks)
        `the days the cat has been kept by the person` MEANS
            IF   null `the person's own`
            THEN Day d MINUS `earliest start of` `current keepings`
            ELSE Day d MINUS `earliest start of` `the person's own`

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 5
GIVEN d   IS A DATE
      p   IS A Person
      cat IS A Cat
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(1) is contravened on` d `by` p `as to` cat IF
        `the law is encoded for` d
    AND `an owner of` cat `on` d `:` p
    AND `reached` 6 `months of age, if born on` (cat's `date of birth`) `, on` d
    AND NOT `registered with the local government of the district where it is ordinarily kept` cat `on` d
    AND NOT `s 5(1) does not apply on` d `to` p `as to` cat

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 5(1) "Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 5(1) — maximum fine` MEANS 5000

§§§§ `6. Cats to wear tags`

-- s 6(2): "Subsection (1) does not apply if the cat belongs to a class of
-- cats prescribed as exempt from wearing registration tags when in a public
-- place." reg 10(2): "The owner of a cat that is being exhibited is exempt
-- from the requirement ... but only while that cat is being exhibited."
-- reg 10(1): "exhibited means exhibited for show purposes at a cat show held
-- by — (a)-(d) [the four bodies]; or (e) a body that is affiliated with an
-- organisation mentioned in paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d)."
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 reg 10
GIVEN o IS AN Occasion
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `being exhibited, within reg 10` o IF
    CONSIDER o's `being exhibited at a show held by`
    WHEN NOTHING                                  THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST (`one of the cat fancy bodies` b)   THEN TRUE      -- (a)-(d)
    WHEN JUST (`a body affiliated with` b)        THEN TRUE      -- (e)
    WHEN JUST `another show organiser`            THEN FALSE

-- s 6(1): "The owner of a registered cat must ensure that when the cat is
-- in a public place the cat is wearing its registration tag."
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 6(1), (2); Cat Regulations 2012 reg 10
GIVEN o   IS AN Occasion
      p   IS A Person
      cat IS A Cat
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 6(1) is contravened on` o `by` p `as to` cat IF
        `the law is encoded for` (o's `date`)
    AND `an owner of` cat `on` (o's `date`) `:` p
    AND `registered` cat `on` (o's `date`)
    AND o's `in a public place`
    AND NOT o's `wearing its registration tag`
    AND NOT "(2)" ... `being exhibited, within reg 10` o

-- s 6(3): "It is a defence to a charge under subsection (1) if the accused
-- establishes that — (a) the contravention ... was due to — (i) the act or
-- default of another person; or (ii) an accident; or (iii) some other cause
-- beyond the accused's control; and (b) the accused took reasonable
-- precautions and could not by the exercise of due diligence have prevented
-- the commission of the offence." Each limb is a finding of fact: inputs.
-- (the type is declared in cat-domain.l4)

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 6(3)
GIVEN f IS A `Section 6(3) findings`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 6(3) defence is established` f IF
        "(a)" ... `the contravention was due to another person, an accident or a cause beyond control`
    AND "(b)" ... `reasonable precautions were taken and due diligence could not have prevented it`
    WHERE
        `the contravention was due to another person, an accident or a cause beyond control` MEANS
                "(i)"   ... f's `due to the act or default of another person`
            ..  "(ii)"  ... f's `due to an accident`
            OR  "(iii)" ... f's `due to some other cause beyond the accused's control`
        `reasonable precautions were taken and due diligence could not have prevented it` MEANS
                f's `took reasonable precautions`
            AND f's `could not by due diligence have prevented it`

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 6(1) "Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 6(1) — maximum fine` MEANS 5000

§§§§ `7. Interference with tag`

-- s 7: "A person must not, without reasonable excuse, remove or interfere
-- with a registration tag worn by a cat."
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 7
GIVEN `removed or interfered with a registration tag worn by a cat` IS A BOOLEAN
      `had a reasonable excuse`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 7 is contravened, where the person` `removed or interfered with a registration tag worn by a cat` `and the excuse is` `had a reasonable excuse` IF
        `removed or interfered with a registration tag worn by a cat`
    AND NOT "without reasonable excuse" ... `had a reasonable excuse`

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 7 "Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 7 — maximum fine` MEANS 5000

§§§ `Subdivision 2 — How to register a cat`

§§§§ `8. Application for registration`

-- s 8(1): "The owner of a cat that is ordinarily kept in the district of a
-- local government may apply to that local government for the grant or
-- renewal of the registration of the cat."
-- s 8(2) and reg 11(1): the application supplies Form 1 Parts A, B, D, F and
-- G and is accompanied by the Schedule 3 fee (cat-regs-sch3-fees.l4).
-- reg 11(2)-(3): on paper or online; online, no signature is required.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 8(1)
GIVEN d   IS A DATE
      p   IS A Person
      cat IS A Cat
      lg  IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may apply on` d `under s 8 by` p `for` cat `to` lg IF
        `the law is encoded for` d
    AND `an owner of` cat `on` d `:` p
    AND cat's `district where ordinarily kept` EQUALS lg

@ref Cat Regulations 2012 reg 11(1)(a)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`reg 11(1)(a) — the parts of Form 1 a registration application supplies` MEANS
    LIST "Part A — Owner details", "Part B — Cat details", "Part D — Registration", "Part F — Previous convictions", "Part G — Declaration"

§§§§ `9. Registration`

-- s 9(2): "A local government must refuse an application for the grant or
-- renewal of the registration of a cat if, and only if, the local government
-- is satisfied that one or more of the following apply — (a) the applicant
-- is a child under 18 years of age; (b) the cat belongs to a class of cats
-- prescribed as exempt from registration; (c) the cat is not microchipped;
-- (d) the cat is not sterilised; (e) the applicant has been convicted within
-- the previous 3 years of 2 or more offences against any of the following —
-- (i) this Act; (ii) the Dog Act 1976; (iii) the Animal Welfare Act 2002."
-- s 9(3): "Despite subsection (2)(c), a local government must not refuse an
-- application ... of a cat that is not microchipped if the cat is exempt from
-- microchipping as referred to in section 14(2)."
-- s 9(4): the same for (2)(d) and s 18(2).
--
-- FORK F-07 (resolved): "an offence against this Act" is an offence against
-- the Act itself, not against regulations or a local law under it. The
-- Interpretation Act s 5 defines "Act" apart from "subsidiary legislation",
-- and Cat Act s 62(1) itself says "against this Act or a regulation or local
-- law made under this Act" when it means both.
-- FORK F-08: "within the previous 3 years" is counted back from the day the
-- application is determined, the day the local government must be satisfied.
-- FORK F-09: (c) and (d) carry no age limit. A kitten under 6 months that is
-- not sterilised cannot be "exempt from sterilisation as referred to in
-- section 18(2)" — a s 18(2)(a) certificate cannot apply under 6 months, and
-- s 18(1)'s age threshold is not an exemption — so its registration must be
-- refused. The Act does not require it to be registered (s 5(1)), so this
-- bites only on a voluntary application.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 9(2)(e)
GIVEN p IS A Person
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of convictions within the previous 3 years of` p `counted on` d MEANS
    count (filter `a counting conviction` (p's `convictions`))
    WHERE
        `a counting conviction` c MEANS
                c's `instrument` EQUALS `the Act itself`
            AND (    "(i)"   ... c's `offence against` EQUALS `the Cat Act 2011`
                 ..  "(ii)"  ... c's `offence against` EQUALS `the Dog Act 1976`
                 OR  "(iii)" ... c's `offence against` EQUALS `the Animal Welfare Act 2002`)
            AND `within the` 36 `months before` d `, an event on` (c's `date of the conviction`)

-- A ground that applies contributes its words to the list; one that does
-- not contributes nothing.
GIVEN ground IS A STRING
      holds  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`ground if` ground holds MEANS
    IF holds THEN LIST ground ELSE EMPTY

DECLARE `Registration determination` IS ONE OF
    `the local government must refuse the application` HAS `the grounds` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `the local government must grant or renew the registration`
    `the local government may refuse to consider the application`     -- s 9(6)

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 9(2)-(4)
GIVEN app    IS A `Registration application`
      cat    IS A Cat
      people IS A LIST OF Person
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the s 9(2) grounds that apply to` app `for` cat `, its owners among` people MEANS
    concat (LIST `(a)`, `(b)`, `(c)`, `(d)`, `(e)`)
    WHERE
        d MEANS app's `date determined`
        `(a)` MEANS
            `ground if` "(a) the applicant is a child under 18 years of age"
                (`under` 18 `years of age, if born on` (app's `applicant`'s `date of birth`) `, on` d)
        `(b)` MEANS
            `ground if` "(b) the cat belongs to a class of cats prescribed as exempt from registration"
                (`belongs to a class of cats prescribed as exempt from registration` cat)
        `(c)` MEANS
            `ground if` "(c) the cat is not microchipped"
                (    NOT `microchipped` cat
                 AND NOT "(3)" ... `exempt from microchipping` cat `on` d)
        `(d)` MEANS
            `ground if` "(d) the cat is not sterilised"
                (    NOT `sterilised` cat
                 AND NOT "(4)" ... `exempt from sterilisation` cat `on` d `, its owners among` people)
        `(e)` MEANS
            `ground if` "(e) the applicant has been convicted within the previous 3 years of 2 or more offences against this Act, the Dog Act 1976 or the Animal Welfare Act 2002"
                (`the number of convictions within the previous 3 years of` (app's `applicant`) `counted on` d AT LEAST 2)

-- s 9(1): "On receiving an application ... a local government is to — (a)
-- grant or refuse to grant the registration of the cat; or (b) renew or
-- refuse to renew the registration of the cat." s 9(5)-(6): if the applicant
-- does not comply in time with a request for documents or information (of
-- not more than 21 days), "The local government may refuse to consider an
-- application".
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 9(1)-(6)
GIVEN app     IS A `Registration application`
      cat     IS A Cat
      people  IS A LIST OF Person
      request IS A MAYBE `Information request`
GIVETH A `Registration determination`
`the s 9 determination of` app `for` cat `, its owners among` people `, after the request` request MEANS
    IF   `the law is encoded for` (app's `date determined`)
    THEN BRANCH IF `the applicant did not comply with a request in time`
                   THEN `the local government may refuse to consider the application`
                IF NOT null `grounds`
                   THEN `the local government must refuse the application` `grounds`
                OTHERWISE `the local government must grant or renew the registration`
    ELSE REFUSE "no source is encoded for a date before 25 September 2025"
    WHERE
        `grounds` MEANS `the s 9(2) grounds that apply to` app `for` cat `, its owners among` people
        `the applicant did not comply with a request in time` MEANS
            CONSIDER request
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST r  THEN     "(5) of not more than 21 days" ... r's `days allowed` AT MOST 21
                              AND NOT r's `complied with in time`

-- s 9(7) and reg 12(1): "Registration of a cat may be for — (a) either one
-- year or 3 years; or (b) for the life of the cat." Every `Registration term`
-- is one of these; reg 12(2)(a) is in cat-part1-preliminary.l4.
-- reg 12(2)(b): registration "may be renewed to take effect as from
-- 1 November in any year, within the preceding period of 21 days" — read with
-- Interpretation Act s 61(1)(c), the 21 days before 1 November not counting
-- 1 November itself: 11 to 31 October.
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 reg 12(2)(b); Interpretation Act 1984 s 61(1)(c)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a renewal may take effect from the next 1 November, if made on` d IF
        d AT LEAST (`the next 1 November` MINUS 21)
    AND d LESS THAN `the next 1 November`
    WHERE
        `the next 1 November` MEANS
            IF   d LESS THAN YMD (DATE_YEAR d) 11 1
            THEN YMD (DATE_YEAR d) 11 1
            ELSE YMD (DATE_YEAR d PLUS 1) 11 1

§§§§ `10. Cancellation of registration`

-- s 10: "A local government may cancel the registration of a cat — (a) if
-- the cat — (i) has died; or (ii) is no longer kept in the State; or (iii)
-- has been registered with another local government; or (b) if the owner of
-- the cat has been convicted within the period of 12 months before the
-- cancellation of 2 or more offences against any of the following — (i) this
-- Act; (ii) the Dog Act 1976; (iii) the Animal Welfare Act 2002."
-- A power: TRUE means the local government MAY cancel, not that it must.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 10
GIVEN cat   IS A Cat
      d     IS A DATE
      owner IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the local government may cancel the registration of` cat `on` d `, its owner being` owner IF
        `the law is encoded for` d
    AND (    "(a)" ...     "(i)"   ... `the cat has died`
                       ..  "(ii)"  ... NOT cat's `kept in the State`
                       OR  "(iii)" ... cat's `registered with another local government since`
         OR  "(b)" ... count (filter `a counting conviction` (owner's `convictions`)) AT LEAST 2)
    WHERE
        `the cat has died` MEANS
            CONSIDER cat's `date of death`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST x  THEN x AT MOST d
        `a counting conviction` c MEANS
                c's `instrument` EQUALS `the Act itself`
            AND (    c's `offence against` EQUALS `the Cat Act 2011`
                 ..  c's `offence against` EQUALS `the Dog Act 1976`
                 OR  c's `offence against` EQUALS `the Animal Welfare Act 2002`)
            AND `within the` 12 `months before` d `, an event on` (c's `date of the conviction`)

§§§§ `11. Registration numbers, certificates and tags`

-- s 11(1): the local government "is to — (a) allot a registration number to
-- the cat; and (b) give the owner of the cat a registration certificate in
-- the prescribed form for the cat; and (c) give the owner of the cat a
-- registration tag ...". reg 14: the certificate is Form 2. s 11(2): a
-- replacement MAY be given for one stolen, lost, damaged or destroyed.
-- reg 15(1): a tag is "(a) marked with a registration number ...; (b) marked
-- with the name of the local government and its contact number; and (c)
-- coloured in the colour representing the year of expiry of the
-- registration". reg 15(2): "A lifetime registration tag is to be coloured
-- orange." reg 15(3): the Minister designates the year colours by Gazette
-- notice — not a source here, so the year's colour is named, not looked up.
DECLARE `Tag colour` IS ONE OF
    `orange`
    `the colour the Minister has designated for the year of expiry` HAS `the year of expiry` IS A NUMBER

@ref Cat Regulations 2012 reg 15(1)(c), (2)
GIVEN r IS A Registration
GIVETH A `Tag colour`
`the colour of the registration tag for` r MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day of the registration period` r
    WHEN NOTHING    THEN `orange`
    WHEN JUST last  THEN `the colour the Minister has designated for the year of expiry` (DATE_YEAR last)

§§§§ `12. Register of cats`

-- s 12(1)-(4): an accurate and up-to-date register, in such form as the local
-- government thinks fit, recording the prescribed information; errors and
-- omissions may be corrected. reg 16 prescribes the information.
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 reg 16
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`reg 16 — information to be recorded in the register` MEANS
    LIST "(a) the cat owner's full name"
       , "(b) the cat owner's residential address"
       , "(c) the cat owner's postal address (if different from the residential address)"
       , "(d) the cat owner's date of birth"
       , "(e) the cat owner's contact telephone numbers — home, work and mobile"
       , "(f) the cat owner's email address"
       , "(g) details of an alternative contact (i.e. if the owner cannot be contacted)"
       , "(h) the address at which the cat is normally kept"
       , "(i) the cat's name"
       , "(j) the cat's registration number"
       , "(k) the cat's sterilisation status"
       , "(l) the cat's microchip number"
       , "(m) the breed (if known), colour and gender of the cat"

§§§§ `13. Notice to be given of certain decisions made under this Subdivision`

-- s 13(1): "Within 7 days after making a decision referred to in subsection
-- (2) the local government is to give to the owner of the cat the subject
-- of the decision, notice in writing of — (a) the decision; and (b) the
-- reasons for the decision; and (c) the person's rights under Part 4
-- Division 5 to object against, and apply for a review of, the decision."
-- s 13(2): "(a) refuse to grant or renew the registration of a cat under
-- section 9; or (b) cancel the registration of a cat under section 10."
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 13(2)
GIVEN dec IS A `Reviewable decision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a decision s 13 applies to` dec IF
        "(a)" ... dec EQUALS `refusal to grant registration`
    ..  "(a)" ... dec EQUALS `refusal to renew registration`
    OR  "(b)" ... dec EQUALS `cancellation of registration`

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 13(1)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor `Act required`
`s 13 — the local government's duty, counted in days from the decision` MEANS
    PARTY `the local government`
    MUST  `give notice of the decision, the reasons and the rights of objection and review`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the local government` BECAUSE "s 13(1): written notice of the decision, the reasons and the rights under Part 4 Division 5 was not given within 7 days after the decision"

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 13(1)
GIVEN d        IS A DATE
      h        IS AN `Objection history`
      holidays IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 13 notice is late, as at` d `, for` h `given` holidays IF
        `the law is encoded for` d
    AND `a decision s 13 applies to` (h's `decision`)
    AND `not done within` 7 `days after` (h's `date of the decision`) `, done on` (h's `date notice of the decision was given`) `, as at` d `given` holidays

§§§ `reg 13. Changes in registration`

-- reg 13: "Where a cat is registered with a local government and the owner
-- moves to another local government area, the owner may notify both the
-- former and the new local government to continue that period of
-- registration with the new local government." A permission to the owner.
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 reg 13
GIVEN d                  IS A DATE
      p                  IS A Person
      cat                IS A Cat
      `the new district` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `under reg 13, on` d `,` p `may ask to continue the registration of` cat `in` `the new district` IF
        `the law is encoded for` d
    AND `registered` cat `on` d
    AND `an owner of` cat `on` d `:` p
    AND CONSIDER cat's `registration`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST r  THEN NOT r's `local government` EQUALS `the new district`
